*> COBOL 2002 made the IDENTIFICATION DIVISION header optional: a
*> program, nested or not, may start at PROGRAM-ID.
PROGRAM-ID. OUTER.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  X                   PIC XX VALUE "OK".
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    CALL "INNER" USING X
    STOP RUN.
PROGRAM-ID. INNER.
DATA DIVISION.
LINKAGE SECTION.
01  Y                   PIC XX.
PROCEDURE DIVISION USING Y.
    MOVE "KO" TO Y
    EXIT PROGRAM.
END PROGRAM INNER.
END PROGRAM OUTER.
PROGRAM-ID. NEXT-ONE.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    GOBACK.
END PROGRAM NEXT-ONE.
